WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
A new bike shop is getting busier.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.090
Money from sales climbs every month:

3
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:10.050
6,000 pounds, then 9,000, then 14,000.

4
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.980
Yet in February, its bank
balance drops below zero:

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.920
minus 1,500 pounds.

6
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.050
And it is not only new shops.

7
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.460
A firm can report a profit and still be

8
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.350
unable to pay its wages.

9
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.660
So how can a business be making a profit

10
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.590
and still run out of money?

11
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:30.040
In this mission, you'll
read a statement of income

12
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.370
and work out three different
profits and their margins.

13
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.390
Then you'll build a cash-flow
forecast and spot the month

14
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.220
when the money runs short.

15
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.680
Your mission: explain how
profit and money in the bank

16
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.730
can tell two different stories.
